cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LureScope: A Deployable Fraud-Lure Scoring API with a Live Adversarial-Evasion Demo"
message: "If you use LureScope in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahamed
    given-names: Imran
    email: immu4989@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/immu4989/lurescope"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/immu4989/lurescope"
abstract: >-
  LureScope is the serving companion to LureBench: an HTTP API and browser demo
  that scores a message for fraud-lure likelihood, applies an adversarial attack,
  and re-scores after an input-normalization defense, making the gap between
  clean-data accuracy and deployment accuracy visible on a single message. It
  reuses LureBench's detectors and attacks directly, so the served model and the
  benchmarked model cannot drift.
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-07-27"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - phishing
  - adversarial robustness
  - model serving
  - AI security
references:
  - type: software
    title: "LureBench: A Benchmark and Evaluation Harness for Detecting AI-Generated Fraud Lures"
    authors:
